    "body": "blocked: waiting on unmerged `#1958` prerequisites `#1962` and `#1966` on `upstream/main`.\n\nChecked `upstream/main` at `e3ca44fa7` and open PRs in `NeoTech/Camcraft`:\n\n- `#1965` (`crates/post/src/kinematics/`) has merged via PR `#2056` (shipped in `v0.22.0`).\n- `#1962` (`.mch` AC trunnion kinematics fields and `controller.rtcp`) is still open (`in-review`); PR `#2162` (`merge-ready`) is not yet merged to `upstream/main`. On `upstream/main`, `crates/post/src/post/machine.rs` still infers `rtcp` geometrically from tilted rotaries and does not carry `pivot`, `offset`, `zero_offset`, `rollover`, `sign_convention`, ordered rotary chain, or `controller.rtcp`.\n- `#1966` (`Add G93 inverse-time feed solver and 3+2 vs simultaneous section markers`) is still open and unclaimed with no PR. On `upstream/main`, `crates/post/src/post/mod.rs` (`Dump`, `dump`) and `crates/app/src/posting.rs` emit no section mode parameter distinguishing 3-axis, 3+2 indexed, and simultaneous 5-axis sections, and `crates/post/src/post/` (`rotary_cap.rs`, `engine.rs`) has no shared Rust `G93` inverse-time feed solver (`F = 1 / dt_min`) or post-IK coordinate/feed wiring.\n\nCompleting `mach4.cps` with 3+2 vs simultaneous separation, pre-compensated `X Y Z A C` + `G93` `F` emission, and missing-trunnion / unexpected `controller.rtcp = true` refusals requires `#1962` and `#1966`; implementing them inside `#1968` would duplicate PR `#2162` and issue `#1966`.\n\nOverlap note for when `#1968` is unblocked: open PRs `#2162`, `#2149`, `#2140`, `#2136`, `#2115`, `#1681`, and `#468` touch `crates/app/src/posting.rs`; none touch `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`.\n\nStopped before claiming (`#1968` left open and unclaimed; added `blocked`; no branch, worktree, code change, or PR created). Drop `blocked` once `#1962` and `#1966` merge to `main`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
